    "notes_unique": "Nuclear testing ground (1946-1958, 67 US nuclear tests on Bikini and Enewetak atolls; Castle Bravo March 1, 1954 largest US test 15 megatons, 1000x Hiroshima, irradiated Rongelap atoll downwind, fallout on islanders, Japanese fishing boat Lucky Dragon #5; Bikini evacuated 1946 'for the good of mankind', residents never permanently returned; Bikini swimsuit named after atoll; Enewetak cleanup 1977-80 Runit Dome/Cactus Dome leaking radioactive waste; intergenerational health effects, birth defects, cancer, Nuclear Claims Tribunal awarded $2.3B but US paid only $150M); Compact of Free Association (COFA, 1986 with US, renewed 2023 for 20 years, $7.1B total, US military access/defence responsibility, Marshallese can live/work/study in US without visa, ~30k in US); Kwajalein Atoll (world's largest coral atoll by lagoon area, Ronald Reagan Ballistic Missile Defense Test Site, US Army, intercontinental missile testing, Ebeye 'slum of the Pacific' ~12k on 78 acres); climate change (average elevation 2m, existential, many islands submerging, some already relocated); stick chart navigation (unique Marshallese innovation, wave/swell patterns on coconut stick frameworks, each chart unique, UNESCO); flag ship registry (3rd largest in world by tonnage, Liberia/Panama/Marshall Islands, source of revenue); Majuro overcrowded (~27k); copra/fisheries economy; US strategic interest (Pacific pivot)",
